===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|Venda}}

# A member of the Black people of this area.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Godfrey Mwakikagile|title=South Africa and Its People|publisher=New Africa Press|isbn=9780981425832|page=176
|text=The '''Venda''' live mostly in Limpopo Province in the northern part of South Africa. There are about one million '''Vendas''' and their language is also known as Luvenda, Tshivenda or simply Venda. Their native land was once a Bantustan during [Apartheid].}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2015-02-01|author=Saloshna Vandeyar|author2=Thirusellvan Vandeyar|title=The Construction, Negotiation, and Representation of Immigrant Student Identities in South African schools|publisher=IAP|isbn=9781623968885|page=63
|text=They don't really react badly, because they say I look mostly like a South African, like a '''Venda'''. I don't look like a foreigner. I mean I look like a '''Venda'''. So, when I tell them I am from another country, they actually get surprised.}}

